qemu-rdp: credentials from a file, and the bus name optional

qemu-rdp offers only NLA (CredSSP), and without credentials it refuses every client. Upstream sets
them with the D-Bus method SetCredentials on the name org.QemuDisplay.RDP, which it requests on the
display's bus and stops without. On Proxmox VE (wsh-pve) every VM's display has a bus of its own
whose policy lets root own org.qemu and nothing else, so qemu-rdp stopped at the start, and the
password would have had to go through a command line (busctl call).

- serve --credentials-file FILE: the user name on the first line, the password on the second, set
  before the server takes its first client. The unit (wsh-qemu-rdp@.service) writes the file into
  the service's runtime directory, readable by the service user alone.
- A refused RequestName is a warning: the server runs; SetCredentials, still exported on
  /org/qemu_display/rdp, just has no well-known name.

For wsh-pve (packages/wsh-qemu-rdp), against qemu-display at the commit upstream.env pins.
